<title>CANADA: Scott's Restaurants sets share buyback.</title>
<headline>Scott's Restaurants sets share buyback.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scott's Restaurants Inc said it planned to buy back up to 1.6 million or some 10 percent of its subordinate voting shares and up to 500,000 or about five percent of its class C shares.</p>
<p>Scott's, which operates KFC restaurants in Canada, may rebuy the shares on the Toronto Stock Exchange between October 2, 1996 and October 1, 1997, it said.</p>
<p>--Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100</p>
